.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A user‑mode barrier that synchronizes multiple threads across repeated phases\&. The barrier waits until a specified number of threads have arrived, then opens and allows all participants to continue\&. After the phase completes, the barrier resets and becomes ready for the next cycle\&. 

The implementation uses two separate locks to keep the logic clean: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRm_hold\fP controls when the barrier is open or closed\&. Threads arriving at the barrier wait until this lock is released\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRm_context\fP protects the phase‑transition logic\&. Only one thread is allowed to perform the phase reset, update counters, apply drops, and invoke the completion callback\&.   
.PP

.PP
Each thread calls \fRArrive()\fP to increment the arrival counter\&. When the counter reaches the required maximum, the barrier opens and all waiting threads proceed\&. Afterward, the barrier resets its counters and prepares for the next phase\&. The optional \fROnComplition\fP callback is invoked whenever a phase finishes\&.

.PP
Because this is a user‑mode barrier, it does not serialize console output\&. Multiple threads may print messages at the same time, causing the text to appear out of order\&. This is normal and does not indicate any problem with the synchronization logic\&. 
